title: A National Left Rally
subtitle: Put one political theme before the whole alliance.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: poland_party_card
view-if: month_actions < max_month_actions and poland_rally_timer <= 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; poland_rally_timer = 2 if pres_2020_active or (year = 2020 and month >= 4 and month <= 7); poland_rally_timer = 6 if not pres_2020_active and not (year = 2020 and month >= 4 and month <= 7)
card-image: img/poland/cards/national-left-rally.webp

= A National Left Rally

The hall can display unity for one evening. Its subject decides which current
believes the party has finally become its own.

- @work
- @equality
- @democracy
- @security
- @local
- @cancel

@work
title: Work, wages and public services
subtitle: Lewica Pracy, union organisers and Razem gain the clearest ownership.
on-arrival: {!
const support = Number(Q.social_spending_support);
const salience = Number(Q.social_spending_salience);
const backlash = Number(Q.social_spending_backlash);
const raw = ((support - 50) / 15 - (backlash - 35) / 45) *
    (0.45 + salience / 100);
const net = Math.round(Math.max(
    -3,
    Math.min(3, raw)
));
const scale = Math.max(0.65, Math.min(1.50, 1 + net * 0.15));
Q.workers_support += Math.max(1, Math.round(3 * scale));
Q.public_sector_support += Math.max(1, Math.round(2 * scale));
Q.labor_credibility += Math.max(1, Math.round(2 * scale));
Q.union_trust += 2;
Q.opzz_cooperation += 1;
Q.labor_mobilization += 2;
Q.labor_dissent -= 3;
Q.razem_dissent -= 3;
Q.barons_dissent += 2;
Q.public_trust += net * 0.35;
Q.public_mood_pending_social_spending_support += net >= 1 ? 2 : (net <= -1 ? -1 : 1);
Q.public_mood_pending_social_spending_salience += 6;
Q.public_mood_pending_social_spending_backlash += net < 0 ? 4 : 2;
Q.card_public_response_score = net;
Q.card_public_response = net >= 2
    ? "breakthrough"
    : (net >= 1
        ? "favourable"
        : (net <= -2
            ? "reversal"
            : (net <= -1 ? "backlash" : "contested")));
Q.public_opinion_last_issue = "Social spending and public services";
Q.public_opinion_last_reception = Q.card_public_response;
Q.public_opinion_last_delta = net;
Q.public_opinion_last_action = "National rally: work and public services";
Q.news_headline = net >= 1
    ? "A popular social offer fills the Left stage"
    : (net <= -1
        ? "The spending rally meets an organised counterattack"
        : "Work and public services fill the Left stage");
!}

[? if card_public_response = "breakthrough": The hall's demands match a public
majority already looking for a political owner. Clips travel far beyond the
party audience, and organisers leave with names rather than applause alone. ?]
[? if card_public_response = "favourable": The social offer lands well. Cost
questions remain, but they do not displace the argument about wages and public
capacity. ?]
[? if card_public_response = "contested": Support is real and so is anxiety
about cost. The rally consolidates the base without yet settling the national
argument. ?]
[? if card_public_response = "backlash": High attention gives spending
opponents an audience of their own. The Left gains committed organisers while
losing some less certain listeners. ?]
[? if card_public_response = "reversal": The message arrives in a hostile,
panicked climate and is framed as an unaffordable promise. Even a strong hall
cannot hide the wider loss. ?]


- #poland_card_finish

@equality
title: Reproductive freedom and equal citizenship
subtitle: Women and younger voters respond; conservative organisers retreat.
on-arrival: {!
const support = (
    Number(Q.abortion_rights_support) +
    Number(Q.lgbt_equality_support) +
    Number(Q.secular_state_support)
) / 3;
const salience = (
    Number(Q.abortion_rights_salience) +
    Number(Q.lgbt_equality_salience) +
    Number(Q.secular_state_salience)
) / 3;
const backlash = (
    Number(Q.abortion_rights_backlash) +
    Number(Q.lgbt_equality_backlash) +
    Number(Q.secular_state_backlash)
) / 3;
const raw = ((support - 50) / 15 - (backlash - 35) / 45) *
    (0.45 + salience / 100);
const net = Math.round(Math.max(
    -3,
    Math.min(3, raw)
));
const scale = Math.max(0.65, Math.min(1.50, 1 + net * 0.15));
Q.women_support += Math.max(1, Math.round(3 * scale));
Q.young_support += Math.max(1, Math.round(2 * scale));
Q.feminist_trust += Math.max(1, Math.round(3 * scale));
Q.progressives_strength += 1;
Q.progressives_dissent -= 3;
Q.spring_dissent -= 2;
Q.barons_dissent += 4;
Q.rural_support -= net < 0 ? 2 : 1;
Q.public_trust += net * 0.30;
for (const issue of [
    "abortion_rights",
    "lgbt_equality",
    "secular_state"
]) {
    Q[issue + "_support"] += net >= 1 ? 1 : (net <= -2 ? -1 : 0);
    Q[issue + "_salience"] += 5;
    Q[issue + "_backlash"] += net < 0 ? 4 : 2;
}
Q.card_public_response_score = net;
Q.card_public_response = net >= 2
    ? "breakthrough"
    : (net >= 1
        ? "favourable"
        : (net <= -2
            ? "reversal"
            : (net <= -1 ? "backlash" : "contested")));
Q.public_opinion_last_issue =
    "Abortion, LGBT equality and secular institutions";
Q.public_opinion_last_reception = Q.card_public_response;
Q.public_opinion_last_delta = net;
Q.public_opinion_last_action = "National rally: equal citizenship";
Q.news_headline = net >= 1
    ? "Equality finds an audience beyond the Left hall"
    : (net <= -1
        ? "Equality becomes the rally and the counter-rally's dividing line"
        : "Equality becomes the rally's dividing line");
!}

[? if card_public_response = "breakthrough": Public attitudes have moved
faster than the cautious wings expected. The rally makes a popular demand look
governable rather than merely symbolic. ?]
[? if card_public_response = "favourable": The case for equal citizenship wins
more agreement than alarm, though conservative organisations immediately begin
their answer. ?]
[? if card_public_response = "contested": The rally sharpens both camps.
Committed supporters are energised; persuadable voters wait to see whether the
programme survives a coalition negotiation. ?]
[? if card_public_response = "backlash": Attention is high but acceptance has
not caught up. The base grows more committed while a louder conservative
counter-mobilisation costs support elsewhere. ?]
[? if card_public_response = "reversal": A hostile climate turns the rally into
evidence for the opposition's culture-war story. Organisational gains cannot
cancel the immediate electoral loss. ?]


- #poland_card_finish

@democracy
title: Courts, elections and democratic institutions
subtitle: Broad opposition appeal with less distinctive social content.
on-arrival: {!
const support = Number(Q.rule_of_law_support);
const salience = Number(Q.rule_of_law_salience);
const backlash = Number(Q.rule_of_law_backlash);
const raw = ((support - 50) / 15 - (backlash - 35) / 45) *
    (0.45 + salience / 100);
const net = Math.round(Math.max(
    -3,
    Math.min(3, raw)
));
const scale = Math.max(0.65, Math.min(1.50, 1 + net * 0.15));
Q.constitutional_restraint += Math.max(1, Math.round(3 * scale));
Q.judicial_legitimacy += Math.max(1, Math.round(3 * scale));
Q.turnout_readiness += Math.max(1, Math.round(3 * scale));
Q.public_trust += 1 + net * 0.35;
Q.ko_relation += 2;
Q.razem_dissent += 1;
Q.public_mood_pending_rule_of_law_support += net >= 1 ? 1 : (net <= -2 ? -1 : 0);
Q.public_mood_pending_rule_of_law_salience += 5;
Q.public_mood_pending_rule_of_law_backlash += net < 0 ? 3 : 1;
Q.card_public_response_score = net;
Q.card_public_response = net >= 2
    ? "breakthrough"
    : (net >= 1
        ? "favourable"
        : (net <= -2
            ? "reversal"
            : (net <= -1 ? "backlash" : "contested")));
Q.public_opinion_last_issue = "Rule-of-law repair";
Q.public_opinion_last_reception = Q.card_public_response;
Q.public_opinion_last_delta = net;
Q.public_opinion_last_action = "National rally: democratic institutions";
Q.news_headline = net >= 1
    ? "Democratic repair becomes a public demand"
    : (net <= -1
        ? "The courts rally falls into a partisan trench"
        : "The Left rallies around democratic institutions");
!}

[? if card_public_response = "breakthrough": Institutional repair has become
both salient and broadly legitimate. The rally converts legal detail into a
democratic mandate. ?]
[? if card_public_response = "favourable": The public hears a defence of fair
rules rather than a lawyers' quarrel. Opposition cooperation gains room. ?]
[? if card_public_response = "contested": Most listeners dislike the crisis,
but they remain divided over who caused it and whose court to trust. ?]
[? if card_public_response = "backlash": The institutional case is swallowed
by partisan identity. Every applause line is answered by an accusation of
revenge. ?]
[? if card_public_response = "reversal": The public sees another elite court
war and punishes the side asking it to pay attention. ?]


- #poland_card_finish

@security
title: A secure border and a humane state
subtitle: Try to hold refugee protection, border control and national security together.
view-if: year >= 2021 or border_security_salience >= 45 or refugee_solidarity_salience >= 45 or national_security_salience >= 50
on-arrival: {!
const support = (
    Number(Q.refugee_solidarity_support) +
    Number(Q.border_security_support) +
    Number(Q.national_security_support)
) / 3;
const salience = (
    Number(Q.refugee_solidarity_salience) +
    Number(Q.border_security_salience) +
    Number(Q.national_security_salience)
) / 3;
const backlash = (
    Number(Q.refugee_solidarity_backlash) +
    Number(Q.border_security_backlash) +
    Number(Q.national_security_backlash)
) / 3;
const compatibilityPenalty = Math.abs(
    Number(Q.border_security_support) -
    Number(Q.refugee_solidarity_support)
) / 35;
const raw = (
    (support - 50) / 15 -
    (backlash - 35) / 45 -
    compatibilityPenalty
) * (0.45 + salience / 100);
const net = Math.round(Math.max(
    -3,
    Math.min(3, raw)
));
const scale = Math.max(0.65, Math.min(1.50, 1 + net * 0.15));
Q.public_trust += net * 0.45;
Q.turnout_readiness += Math.max(1, Math.round(2 * scale));
Q.rural_support += Math.max(0, Math.round(2 * scale));
Q.minority_safety += net >= 0 ? 2 : -1;
Q.border_security_confidence += Math.max(1, Math.round(2 * scale));
Q.military_trust += net >= 0 ? 1 : 0;
for (const issue of [
    "refugee_solidarity",
    "border_security",
    "national_security"
]) {
    Q[issue + "_support"] += net >= 1 ? 1 : (net <= -2 ? -1 : 0);
    Q[issue + "_salience"] += 5;
    Q[issue + "_backlash"] += net < 0 ? 4 : 1;
}
Q.card_public_response_score = net;
Q.card_public_response = net >= 2
    ? "breakthrough"
    : (net >= 1
        ? "favourable"
        : (net <= -2
            ? "reversal"
            : (net <= -1 ? "backlash" : "contested")));
Q.public_opinion_last_issue =
    "Refugees, the Belarus border and national security";
Q.public_opinion_last_reception = Q.card_public_response;
Q.public_opinion_last_delta = net;
Q.public_opinion_last_action = "National rally: security and protection";
Q.news_headline = net >= 1
    ? "Security and refugee protection share one stage"
    : (net <= -1
        ? "The border message satisfies neither frightened camp"
        : "The Left tests a secure and humane border message");
!}

[? if card_public_response = "breakthrough": The public accepts that guarding
the frontier and treating people lawfully are compatible duties. A space opens
between denial and panic. ?]
[? if card_public_response = "favourable": The balanced line reassures more
voters than it alienates. Border personnel remain legitimate without making
refugees into an enemy population. ?]
[? if card_public_response = "contested": The words survive, but each audience
emphasises a different half. The Left has a line, not yet a consensus. ?]
[? if card_public_response = "backlash": Refugee panic and security anxiety
pull in opposite directions. Opponents clip one sentence for softness and the
next for cruelty. ?]
[? if card_public_response = "reversal": Polarisation makes a balanced message
look evasive to every camp. The attempt costs trust without calming fear. ?]


- #poland_card_finish

@local
title: Let every region speak to its own material concerns
subtitle: Less national clarity; stronger county and small-city organisation.
on-arrival: local_network += 4; rural_support += 2; pensioner_support += 1; barons_dissent -= 2; party_unity += 1; media_capacity -= 1; news_headline = "A patchwork rally gives the regions the microphone"


Twelve halls instead of one, each with its own subject: a hospital here, a bus
route there, a factory closure somewhere else. The county organisations end the
week stronger and the national press has nothing to lead with.

- #poland_card_finish


@cancel
title: Cancel the rally and preserve organisational energy
subtitle: No faction wins the stage; no audience sees unity.
on-arrival: organiser_energy += 1; public_trust -= 1; news_headline = "The national rally quietly leaves the calendar"


The organisers keep their energy and the party keeps its unresolved argument.
Nobody has to be told their theme lost, and nobody outside the building sees
the Left do anything at all this month.

- #poland_card_finish
